# go.work.example — OPTIONAL local development workspace.
#
# This file is a template, not an active workspace file. It must NOT be
# committed as go.work (go.work and go.work.sum are gitignored) and it is not
# required to build, test or release wlvision.
#
# Expected sibling checkout layout:
#
#   <parent>/
#   ├── wlvision/          module github.com/bnema/wlvision
#   ├── wlturbo/           module github.com/bnema/wlturbo          (required sibling)
#   └── libwldevices-go/   module github.com/bnema/libwldevices-go  (required sibling)
#
# Copy this file to go.work when you want the Go tool to resolve both sibling
# modules from your working tree without touching any committed go.mod, e.g.:
#
#   cp go.work.example go.work
#   go work sync   # optional
#
# The scripts in scripts/ are the supported workflow and do not need go.work:
#   scripts/use-local-deps.sh      add the ../wlturbo and ../libwldevices-go replaces
#   scripts/check-local-deps.sh    verify those replaces are active
#   scripts/check-release-modules.sh   verify no replace is active (release guard)
#   scripts/clear-local-deps.sh    remove the replaces again
#
# Remember to delete go.work before running the release guard if you created it.

go 1.27

use (
	.
	../wlturbo
	../libwldevices-go
)
